s, depot]\n    if current_node == depot:\n        # Start with nearest-to-depot sweep: smallest radial distance wins\n        return int(unvisited_nodes[np.argmin(to_depot)])\n\n    # Angular detour: use law of cosines with distances only\n    stem = distance_matrix[current_node, depot]\n    a = stem\n    b = to_depot\n    c = cur\n    denom = 2.0 * np.sqrt(np.maximum(a * b, 1e-12))\n    cos_theta = np.clip((a * a + b * b - c * c) / denom, -1.0, 1.0)\n    # Detour grows with (1 - cos_theta); prefer continuing the sweep\n    detour = 1.0 - cos_theta\n    # Reward filling the vehicle: prefer high demand relative to remaining capacity\n    dem = demands[unvisited_nodes]\n    fill = dem / (rest_capacity + dem + 1e-12)\n    # Normalize radial distance by max in candidate set to keep scale-free\n    rmax = np.max(b) + 1e-12\n    radial = b / rmax\n\n    score = 0.7 * detour + 0.6 * radial - 0.4 * fill\n    return int(unvisited_nodes[np.argmin(score)])","code_sha256":"73a1f19d233447606a7711699cd1a063a23c8a63eee7d2adec734403bfd4f954","elapsed_seconds":0.219,"error_code":null,"error_detail":null,"evaluation_id":"1179f2e25cca4bbd88f0d1dd268b166a","generation_parents":[{"algorithm":"Replace the pure savings-per-distance score with a Clarke-Wright-style savings normalized by a blend of distance-to-current and depot-return distance, so customers that reduce total route length are chosen without the previous scale-sensitive ratio behaviour.","code_sha256":"81d07aa1f0b3fa3ffeaf2e35d3da13640b1801a2166ed0b1581e42ed260fe660","population_member_indices":[1],"selected_parent_position":0},{"algorithm":"Replace the pure savings-per-distance score with a Clarke-Wright-style savings normalized by a blend of distance-to-current and depot-return distance, so customers that reduce total route length are chosen without the previous scale-sensitive ratio behaviour.","code_sha256":"81d07aa1f0b3fa3ffeaf2e35d3da13640b1801a2166ed0b1581e42ed260fe660","population_member_indices":[1],"selected_parent_